    "diagnosis": "Hereditary colorectal cancer and polyposis predisposition syndromes and their associated genes (syndrome and genes in blue column)",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The tumour mutation signatures, as defined by COSMIC (the Catalogue of Somatic Mutations in Cancer), that are the primary signatures associated with each defective gene (signatures in green column) are shown. Germline pathogenic variants in the DNA mismatch repair genes (Lynch syndrome) predispose to tumours with high levels of ID2 and ID7. Tumours with mutations in the exonuclease domain of the <em>POLE</em> or <em>POLD1</em> genes demonstrate high levels of SBS10a and SBS10b or SBS10c and SBS10d, a characteristic seen in PPAP-related tumours. Germline biallelic pathogenic variants in the <em>MUTYH</em> gene (MAP) predispose to tumours with high levels of SBS18 and SBS36. Germline biallelic pathogenic variants in <em>NTHL1</em> (NAP) predispose to tumours with high levels of SBS30. Germline biallelic pathogenic variants in <em>MBD4</em> (MANS) predispose to tumours with high levels of SBS1. ID,&nbsp;small insertions and deletions; MANS, <em>MBD4</em>-associated neoplasia syndrome; MAP, <em>MUTYH</em>-associated polyposis; NAP, <em>NTHL1</em>-associated polyposis; PPAP, polymerase proofreading&ndash;associated polyposis; SBS, single-base substitution.",
